  "query_preview": "..Today through Friday...We remain in a quiet weather\npattern through the rest of the week. A weak disturbance will \ndive southward along the west coast over the Baja peninsula \ntoday, but this will bring minimal impacts to northern Arizona \nsave for some upper level clouds. Ridging will continue to build \nfrom the west on Thursday and into the weekend, with temperatures \neventually peaking at 5-10 degrees above normal. Overall expect \ngradually warming temperatures, light winds, and fully dry \nconditions each day through Friday. Expect pleasant weather for \nthe Thanksgiving holiday!\n\nSaturday through Monday...By Saturday, ridging to our west starts to \nretreat and a series of shortwaves will begin to brush past northern \nArizona. The ensemble consensus is for these disturbances to remain \nmostly dry, with the primary impacts being periods of breezy \nwesterly winds and a slight cooling trend for those west of the \nMogollon Rim. \n\nTuesday and onward...There is potential for a more impactful trough \nto move across northern Arizona towards the middle of next week, \nhowever guidance varies considerably on the timing/impacts of this \nsystem. The current forecast calls for precipitation chances to \nreturn by Tuesday evening, but there is plenty of room for this to \nchange with future updates. Stay tuned!",
